       "text": "I didn't enter this order. Amlodipine's labeled maximum for adults is 10 mg once daily, and 50 mg is five times that. Nothing in the patient details you gave (normal kidney and liver function, 70 kg) would justify a dose that high. An overdose could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Possible typo:** If you meant 5 mg once daily (the usual starting dose) or 10 mg once daily (the maximum), I can enter either one right away.\n- **Inadequate blood pressure control:** If 10 mg isn't enough, the usual next step is to add another agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide-like diuretic, instead of raising the amlodipine dose.\n- **Other intent:** If this order is for something else, please tell me and I'll help figure out the right approach. Pharmacy or the prescriber can also review it.\n\nWhich dose would you like me to enter?"
